    "exact_replacements": {
      "Nondominated legal candidates are retained on comparable coordinates. Four-axis quality projections preserve printed-CPD uncertainty and cannot establish five-dimensional dominance when time is unknown. Versions, convergence and repair opportunities remain explicit.": "Nondominated archives bind versions and opportunities. Quality projections cannot establish quality/time dominance when complete cost is unknown.",
      "The controller distinguishes candidate construction, transaction acceptance and final selection. A private intermediate may consume slack or occupy a resource that a later restoration releases; it need not improve CPD on its own. Only a complete checked candidate becomes an observation or committed state. A fixed terminal policy then selects among eligible observed states from that same execution, without borrowing a route from another experiment.": "Construction, transaction acceptance and terminal selection are separate. Private intermediates may spend slack or capacity; only complete checked candidates become observations or commits. The fixed terminal rule selects eligible states from that execution.",
      "The supported claims are therefore specific: complete BNN resource/time tradeoffs, positive and negative circuit/topology transfer, and matched local mechanism effects. Broad superiority of the fully integrated controller, timing-closure guarantees, silicon-area savings and statistical acceleration are not established.": "The evidence supports specific complete-flow tradeoffs and local mechanisms, not broad controller superiority, timing-closure guarantees or statistical acceleration.",
      "Every elapsed time belongs to one declared command and output. Cold graph construction and explicitly supplied reusable indexes are different cost modes. Shared-machine concurrency and OS caches are uncontrolled. After version stability, the matched arms require same-environment interleaved repetitions, including failures, rather than selecting the fastest observation. Recovery segments, component cores and one-time research validation are reported separately and never summed into a fabricated complete time.": "Every time binds one command/output. Cold preparation and reusable indexes are different modes. Shared-host concurrency/caches are uncontrolled; stable matched arms require interleaved repetitions including failures. Recovery, cores and research validation stay separate from complete cost."
